<?xml version="1.0"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSim.xsl"?>
<!--
  Delta-38 - JSBSim FDM v2.0
  Tailless delta-wing UAV, pusher piston engine, catapult launched.

  BUILT FROM: "uav jsbsim questionnaire v3_13-08-26.docx" - every number the
  manufacturer answered is used verbatim and tagged [Q x.y] with the
  questionnaire item it came from.  Everything else is DERIVED (tagged [DER])
  or an ENGINEERING ESTIMATE (tagged [EST]) - see MODEL-NOTES.md for the
  derivation of each and DATA-GAPS.md for what would replace the estimates.

  Coordinate system (as specified in [Q 2.10]):
    x = 0 at the tip of the nose fairing, x increases toward the tail
    y + = starboard,  z + = up
  (JSBSim converts this structural frame to its own body frame internally.)

  PLANFORM [DER from Q 2.1/2.2/2.3/2.9]
    S=1.75 m2, b=1.68 m => AR=1.613 (true slender delta)
    Root chord = 1.79 m (apex at the nose datum, straight unswept trailing
      edge at x=1.79 - the only planform consistent with Q 2.9 and Q 2.1-2.3),
      tip chord 0.293 m, taper 0.164
    LE sweep 60.7 deg, c/4 sweep 53.2 deg
    MAC = 1.221 m (manufacturer states 1.243 - 1.8% apart, within the
      measurement spread of a hand-measured delta; the manufacturer's value is
      used for <chord> so the reference length matches their data sheet)
    x_LEMAC = 0.569 m, y_MAC = 0.319 m

  MASS [Q 3.2/3.3/3.4/3.9/3.10/4.12/4.13]
    empty (airframe+engine+avionics) 15.5 kg @ x=1.370  => structure-only
      13.3 kg @ x=1.3005 once the 2.2 kg engine is broken out as a pointmass
    payload 14.9 kg @ x=0.600, fuel 5.5 L = 3.96 kg @ x=0.976
    typical all-up 34.36 kg (MTOW 38 kg leaves 3.6 kg of payload growth)
    CG 0.991 m, and it moves only +1.9 mm as the tank empties - the tank sits
      essentially on the CG, which is a genuinely good design point.

  STABILITY - READ THIS
    The neutral point of a slender delta is NOT at 25% MAC.  Estimates for
    AR=1.61, LE sweep 60.7 deg span x_ac = 0.566..0.667 root chord, i.e. a
    static margin anywhere from +1.8% to +16.6% MAC against the given CG.
    This model adopts x_ac = 0.615*cr = 1.101 m (SM = 9.0% MAC), the middle of
    that band.  It is the single largest uncertainty in the model - see
    DATA-GAPS.md item 1.  The neutral point sets the VALUE of Cma only; AERORP
    itself is placed ON THE CG, for the reason spelled out at the AERORP
    element below.
-->
<fdm_config name="Delta-38" version="2.0" release="BETA"
   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
   xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSim.xsd">

 <fileheader>
  <author>Derived from uav jsbsim questionnaire v3 (13-08-26)</author>
  <filecreationdate>2026-08-26</filecreationdate>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <description>Delta-38: 38 kg MTOW tailless delta UAV, pusher piston, catapult launch</description>
 </fileheader>

 <metrics>
  <wingarea  unit="M2"> 1.75  </wingarea>   <!-- [Q 2.1] -->
  <wingspan  unit="M">  1.68  </wingspan>   <!-- [Q 2.2] -->
  <chord     unit="M">  1.243 </chord>      <!-- [Q 2.3] MAC -->
  <wing_incidence unit="DEG"> 3.0 </wing_incidence> <!-- [Q 2.4]; folded into CL0, see LIFT -->
  <htailarea unit="M2"> 0.00  </htailarea>  <!-- [Q 2.5] pure delta, no h-tail -->
  <htailarm  unit="M">  0.00  </htailarm>   <!-- [Q 2.6] -->
  <vtailarea unit="M2"> 0.150 </vtailarea>  <!-- [Q 2.7] total winglet area -->
  <!-- [DER] Q 2.8 was left blank. Winglets sit at the wingtips; their ac is at
       25% of the tip chord => x = 1.497 + 0.25*0.293 = 1.570 m, arm to the CG
       (0.991) = 0.579 m. -->
  <vtailarm  unit="M">  0.579 </vtailarm>

  <!--
    AERORP IS DELIBERATELY AT THE CG, NOT AT THE NEUTRAL POINT.

    JSBSim applies the LIFT/DRAG/SIDE forces at AERORP and then adds r x F
    about the CG on top of whatever the PITCH/ROLL/YAW <axis> functions
    produce (FGAerodynamics::Calculate: "vMoments += vDXYZcg*vForces", where
    vDXYZcg is the AERORP-to-CG offset). So if AERORP sits at the neutral point
    AND the model carries a Cma term, the static pitch stability is counted
    TWICE.

    That is not a theoretical worry, it was measured. With AERORP at the
    estimated neutral point of 1.101 m, i.e. 0.110 m behind the CG, ~245 N of
    lift in the post-launch climb-out generated an extra -27 N*m of nose-down
    moment against the +34 N*m the aero functions were producing. Net pitching
    moment about zero: the aircraft would not rotate out of the launch mush no
    matter how much elevon ArduPilot commanded, and it flew into the ground
    about 4 s after every launch. (The Geran-2 model has the same double count,
    AERORP 1.698 m against a CG of 1.433 m, which is very likely part of why it
    needs such an extreme launch speed to get away.)

    With AERORP on the CG, r x F is zero and Cma = -0.156/rad is the whole
    story, which is exactly what the derivative set below was computed for. The
    estimated neutral point (0.615*root chord = 1.101 m) still sets the VALUE
    of Cma - see aero/moment/Pitch_alpha and DATA-GAPS.md item 1 - it just must
    not also be the force application point.

    The CG moves only 1.9 mm as the tank empties, so one fixed value is exact
    enough for the whole flight.
  -->
  <location name="AERORP" unit="M">
   <x> 0.991 </x>
   <y> 0.000 </y>
   <z> 0.000 </z>
  </location>

  <!-- [Q 2.11] measured IMU position. SITL reads its simulated accelerometer
       here (FGAuxiliary vPilotAccel), so the real offset is honoured. -->
  <location name="EYEPOINT" unit="M">
   <x>  1.327 </x>
   <y> -0.017 </y>
   <z> -0.044 </z>
  </location>

  <location name="VRP" unit="M">
   <x> 0.00 </x>
   <y> 0.00 </y>
   <z> 0.00 </z>
  </location>
 </metrics>

 <mass_balance>
  <!--
    MASS BUDGET (x from the nose datum)
      structure+avionics  13.30 kg @ 1.3005   [Q3.3 15.5 minus the engine]
      engine (pointmass)   2.20 kg @ 1.790    [Q3.9]
      payload (pointmass) 14.90 kg @ 0.600    [Q3.10]
      fuel (tank)          3.96 kg @ 0.976    [Q4.12/4.13, 5.5 L MOGAS]
      =====================================
      total               34.36 kg,  CG = 0.9907 m
    Empty CG (no fuel/payload) is 1.370 m [Q 3.4]; the model reproduces it
    exactly because the structural CG above is back-solved from it.

    INERTIA [DER] - Q 3.5-3.7 were answered "0" (= let the tool estimate).

    IMPORTANT: JSBSim treats <ixx>/<iyy>/<izz> as the BASE inertia of the
    <emptywt> structure about the structural CG, and ADDS the parallel-axis
    (transfer) terms of every pointmass and tank on top. So only the
    structure's own inertia goes here; putting the TOTAL in would count the
    transfer terms twice. JSBSim's own Mass Properties Report is the check:
    it must print a total Iyy of ~9.4 slug-ft2 = 12.7 kg*m2.

    Structure = 13.3 kg spread over the 1.79 x 1.68 m delta plate:
      Ixx = m*b^2/24  = 13.3*2.8224/24 = 1.56
      Iyy = m*cr^2/18 = 13.3*3.2041/18 = 2.37   (triangular chordwise mass
                                                 distribution, variance cr^2/18)
      Izz = Ixx + Iyy = 3.93                    (flat-plate relation)
    plus the payload's own body inertia (0.5 m long, 0.25 m dia: 0.23/0.37/0.37)
    and small terms for the fuel and the engine:
      => base Ixx 1.82, Iyy 2.79, Izz 4.35
    JSBSim then adds the transfer terms (Ixx 0.03, Iyy 4.98, Izz 4.96) for a
    total of Ixx 1.85, Iyy 7.77, Izz 9.31 kg*m2. Radii of gyration
    k_x/b = 0.14 and k_y/L = 0.27, both normal for a delta.

    Ixz = 0 per [Q 3.8] (symmetric airframe); the point-mass sum gives
    -0.14 kg*m2, small enough that the manufacturer's answer is kept.
  -->
  <ixx unit="KG*M2"> 1.82 </ixx>
  <iyy unit="KG*M2"> 2.79 </iyy>
  <izz unit="KG*M2"> 4.35 </izz>
  <ixz unit="KG*M2"> 0.00 </ixz>

  <emptywt unit="KG"> 13.30 </emptywt>
  <location name="CG" unit="M">
   <x> 1.3005 </x>   <!-- structure-only CG, back-solved from Q 3.4 -->
   <y> 0.0000 </y>
   <z> 0.0000 </z>
  </location>

  <pointmass name="Payload">
   <description>[Q 3.10] 14.9 kg mission payload in the forward bay</description>
   <weight unit="KG"> 14.90 </weight>
   <location name="POINTMASS" unit="M">
    <x> 0.600 </x>
    <y> 0.000 </y>
    <z> 0.021 </z>
   </location>
  </pointmass>

  <pointmass name="Engine">
   <description>[Q 3.9] 2.2 kg engine, aft (pusher)</description>
   <weight unit="KG"> 2.20 </weight>
   <location name="POINTMASS" unit="M">
    <x>  1.790 </x>
    <y>  0.000 </y>
    <z> -0.010 </z>
   </location>
  </pointmass>
 </mass_balance>

 <ground_reactions>
  <!--
    [EST] No landing gear [Q 7.2]: catapult launch, belly recovery.  These
    STRUCTURE contacts only stop the aircraft falling through the ground.
    Spring/damping scaled to 34 kg (Geran-2's 10000 N/m is sized for 200 kg):
    337 N over three contacts at 4000 N/m = ~28 mm static deflection.
    SKID_AFT sits at z=-0.27, just below the propeller tip (z=-0.264, see
    DATA-GAPS.md item 4 - the questionnaire gives no belly depth, so on the
    numbers supplied the prop is the lowest point of the aircraft).
  -->
  <contact type="STRUCTURE" name="BELLY_FWD">
   <location unit="M"> <x>0.35</x> <y>0.00</y> <z>-0.10</z> </location>
   <static_friction>  0.8 </static_friction>
   <dynamic_friction> 0.5 </dynamic_friction>
   <rolling_friction> 0.5 </rolling_friction>
   <spring_coeff  unit="N/M">   4000 </spring_coeff>
   <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC"> 800 </damping_coeff>
   <max_steer unit="DEG"> 0 </max_steer>
   <brake_group> NONE </brake_group>
  </contact>
  <contact type="STRUCTURE" name="BELLY_MID">
   <location unit="M"> <x>0.99</x> <y>0.00</y> <z>-0.12</z> </location>
   <static_friction>  0.8 </static_friction>
   <dynamic_friction> 0.5 </dynamic_friction>
   <rolling_friction> 0.5 </rolling_friction>
   <spring_coeff  unit="N/M">   4000 </spring_coeff>
   <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC"> 800 </damping_coeff>
   <max_steer unit="DEG"> 0 </max_steer>
   <brake_group> NONE </brake_group>
  </contact>
  <contact type="STRUCTURE" name="SKID_AFT">
   <location unit="M"> <x>1.75</x> <y>0.00</y> <z>-0.27</z> </location>
   <static_friction>  0.8 </static_friction>
   <dynamic_friction> 0.5 </dynamic_friction>
   <rolling_friction> 0.5 </rolling_friction>
   <spring_coeff  unit="N/M">   4000 </spring_coeff>
   <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC"> 800 </damping_coeff>
   <max_steer unit="DEG"> 0 </max_steer>
   <brake_group> NONE </brake_group>
  </contact>
  <contact type="STRUCTURE" name="WINGTIP_L">
   <location unit="M"> <x>1.60</x> <y>-0.84</y> <z>0.00</z> </location>
   <static_friction>  0.8 </static_friction>
   <dynamic_friction> 0.5 </dynamic_friction>
   <rolling_friction> 0.5 </rolling_friction>
   <spring_coeff  unit="N/M">   2000 </spring_coeff>
   <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC"> 400 </damping_coeff>
   <max_steer unit="DEG"> 0 </max_steer>
   <brake_group> NONE </brake_group>
  </contact>
  <contact type="STRUCTURE" name="WINGTIP_R">
   <location unit="M"> <x>1.60</x> <y>0.84</y> <z>0.00</z> </location>
   <static_friction>  0.8 </static_friction>
   <dynamic_friction> 0.5 </dynamic_friction>
   <rolling_friction> 0.5 </rolling_friction>
   <spring_coeff  unit="N/M">   2000 </spring_coeff>
   <damping_coeff unit="N/M/SEC"> 400 </damping_coeff>
   <max_steer unit="DEG"> 0 </max_steer>
   <brake_group> NONE </brake_group>
  </contact>
 </ground_reactions>

 <propulsion>
  <engine file="uav_engine">                    <!-- [Q 4.2] name -->
   <location unit="M">                          <!-- [Q 4.4] -->
    <x>  1.790 </x>
    <y>  0.000 </y>
    <z> -0.010 </z>
   </location>
   <orient unit="DEG">                          <!-- [Q 4.6] straight, 0/0/0 -->
    <pitch>0</pitch> <roll>0</roll> <yaw>0</yaw>
   </orient>
   <feed> 0 </feed>                             <!-- [Q 4.7] single tank -->
   <thruster file="uav_prop">                   <!-- [Q 4.8] name -->
    <location unit="M">                         <!-- [Q 4.9] = overall length -->
     <x>  2.070 </x>
     <y>  0.000 </y>
     <z> -0.010 </z>
    </location>
    <orient unit="DEG">
     <pitch>0</pitch> <roll>0</roll> <yaw>0</yaw>
    </orient>
    <sense>   -1 </sense>       <!-- [Q 4.10] left-hand (counter-clockwise from behind) -->
    <p_factor> 2 </p_factor>    <!-- [EST] Q 4.11 left to the engineer; typical single pusher -->
   </thruster>
  </engine>

  <!-- [Q 4.12/4.13] single 5.5 L tank on the CG. MOGAS A-95: 0.72 kg/L
       => 3.96 kg = 8.73 lb, density 6.01 lb/US-gal. -->
  <tank type="FUEL" number="0">
   <location unit="M">
    <x>  0.976 </x>
    <y>  0.000 </y>
    <z> -0.070 </z>
   </location>
   <capacity unit="LBS"> 8.73 </capacity>
   <contents unit="LBS"> 8.73 </contents>
   <density  unit="LBS/GAL"> 6.01 </density>
  </tank>
 </propulsion>

 <!-- Elevon mixer (no rudder - [Q 7.3] no flaps, delta with elevons only).
      Outputs consumed by <aerodynamics> below:
        fcs/elevator-pos-rad = symmetric elevon (pitch), +/-20 deg
        fcs/aileron-pos-rad  = differential elevon (roll), +/-15 deg -->
 <system file="Aircraft control"/>

 <flight_control name="FCS: Delta-38">
  <!-- all channels live in Systems/Aircraft control.xml -->
 </flight_control>

 <aerodynamics>
  <!--
    Reference: S=1.75 m2, b=1.68 m, c=1.243 m, AR=1.613, LE sweep 60.7 deg

    CLalpha  Helmbold (1942) low-AR swept formula, as used for the Geran-2:
             2*pi*AR / (2 + sqrt(4 + AR^2*(1+tan^2(60.7deg)))) = 1.731 /rad
    CL0      = CLalpha * 3 deg wing incidence [Q 2.4] = 0.091
    CLmax    back-solved from VS1 = 88 km/h at MTOW 38 kg [Q 3.1/3.2]:
             CLmax = 2*W/(rho*V^2*S) = 0.582, reached at alpha = 16.3 deg.
             The table continues past that into the vortex-lift region
             (Polhamus, NASA TR R-394) where a delta peaks near 40 deg.
    Damping derivatives are all NEGATIVE by construction.
  -->

  <!-- =============================== LIFT =============================== -->
  <axis name="LIFT">

   <function name="aero/force/Lift_alpha">
    <description>CL(alpha): CL0=0.091, CLa=1.731/rad (Helmbold), CLmax=0.582 at 16.3 deg (from VS1), vortex lift beyond</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <table>
      <independentVar lookup="row">aero/alpha-rad</independentVar>
      <tableData>
       -0.873  -0.600
       -0.524  -0.500
       -0.349  -0.420
       -0.175  -0.212
        0.000   0.091   <!-- CL0 from the +3 deg wing setting angle -->
        0.087   0.242
        0.175   0.394
        0.284   0.582   <!-- VS1 point: CLmax(practical) at 16.3 deg -->
        0.349   0.680   <!-- vortex-lift onset -->
        0.436   0.790
        0.524   0.890
        0.611   0.960
        0.698   1.000   <!-- vortex-lift peak, ~40 deg -->
        0.785   0.940
        0.873   0.820
        1.047   0.600
        1.571   0.000
      </tableData>
     </table>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/force/Lift_pitch_rate">
    <description>CLq=1.10/rad (tailless delta; DATCOM 5.2.1.1)</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>velocities/q-aero-rad_sec</property>
     <property>aero/ci2vel</property>
     <value> 1.10 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/force/Lift_alpha_rate">
    <description>CLadot=0.35/rad (Nelson, Flight Stability 2.5)</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>aero/alphadot-rad_sec</property>
     <property>aero/ci2vel</property>
     <value> 0.35 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/force/Lift_elevon">
    <description>[EST] CLde=0.55/rad. Elevon geometry is NOT in the questionnaire
    (it flags CLde as uncovered); assumed 22% chord over 20-80% semi-span
    => S_flap/S = 0.13, flapped wing area 0.60 S. DATCOM 6.1.1.2.</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>fcs/elevator-pos-rad</property>
     <value> 0.55 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

  </axis>

  <!-- =============================== DRAG =============================== -->
  <axis name="DRAG">

   <function name="aero/force/Drag_zero_lift">
    <description>[EST] CD0=0.032. Cf(Re=2.8e6)=0.0037 turbulent, form factor
    1.25, Swet/S=2.1 gives 0.0097 clean; the rest is the exposed cylinder head
    /cooling, the engine fairing, the pusher pylon, winglets, antennas and a
    belly launch rail fitting. Raymer 12.3 build-up for a small UAV.</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <value> 0.032 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/force/Drag_induced">
    <description>CDi = k*CL^2, k = 1/(pi*e*AR) = 1/(pi*0.70*1.613) = 0.282 (Anderson 5.3)</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>aero/cl-squared</property>
     <value> 0.282 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/force/Drag_beta">
    <description>Sideslip drag, symmetric in beta (DATCOM 4.2.2.1)</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <table>
      <independentVar lookup="row">aero/beta-rad</independentVar>
      <tableData>
       -1.571  1.000
       -0.524  0.090
       -0.262  0.035
        0.000  0.000
        0.262  0.035
        0.524  0.090
        1.571  1.000
      </tableData>
     </table>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/force/Drag_elevon">
    <description>CDde = 0.012*|de| (DATCOM 6.1.5.1)</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <abs><property>fcs/elevator-pos-rad</property></abs>
     <value> 0.012 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

  </axis>

  <!-- =============================== SIDE =============================== -->
  <axis name="SIDE">

   <function name="aero/force/Side_beta">
    <description>CYb=-0.22/rad. Winglets 0.150 m2 [Q 2.7] with CLa_wl~2.5/rad
    and sidewash efficiency 0.8 give -0.17; the body adds ~-0.05.</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>aero/beta-rad</property>
     <value> -0.22 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/force/Side_yaw_rate">
    <description>CYr=+0.15/rad (Nelson 2.6)</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
     <property>velocities/r-aero-rad_sec</property>
     <value> 0.15 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

  </axis>

  <!-- =============================== PITCH ============================== -->
  <axis name="PITCH">

   <function name="aero/moment/Pitch_zero">
    <description>Cm0=+0.016 (reflexed trailing edge), sized so the aircraft
    trims hands-off at 34 m/s: alpha_trim = Cm0/-Cma = 6.0 deg.</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
     <value> 0.016 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/moment/Pitch_alpha">
    <description>Cma = CLa*(x_cg-x_np)/MAC = 1.731*(0.991-1.101)/1.221
    = -0.156/rad. NEGATIVE = statically stable, SM = 9.0% MAC.
    THE most uncertain number in this model - see DATA-GAPS.md item 1.</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
     <property>aero/alpha-rad</property>
     <value> -0.156 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/moment/Pitch_elevon">
    <description>Cmde = -CLde * arm/MAC = -0.55*(1.676-0.991)/1.221 = -0.309/rad.
    Positive de (TE down) = nose down, so the value is negative by JSBSim sign
    convention. Mach taper is irrelevant below M=0.15 but kept for safety.</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
     <property>fcs/elevator-pos-rad</property>
     <value> -0.309 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/moment/Pitch_damping">
    <description>Cmq=-3.00/rad (tailless delta, DATCOM 5.2.1.2; MUST be negative).
    Deliberately at the strong end of the -2.2..-3.5 estimate band because the
    static margin is only 9% MAC: pitch damping is what keeps the short-period
    well behaved when Cma is weak.</description>
    <product>
     <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
     <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
     <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
     <property>aero/ci2vel</property>
     <property>velocities/q-aero-rad_sec</property>
     <value> -3.00 </value>
    </product>
   </function>

   <function name="aero/moment/Pitch_alphadot">
